occupationalSummary:
&lt;p&gt;This occupation is found in the construction and built environment industry including new-build, renovation and refurbishment.&amp;nbsp; It is a specialist contracting occupation involved in the construction of partitions, walls and ceilings.&amp;nbsp; The Interior Systems sector alone has over 35,000 operatives working on diverse projects in hotels, schools, airports, football stadiums, hospitals, shopping centres.&amp;nbsp; Other projects may mean working on security controlled installations such as military bases which are not usually accessible to the public.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The broad purpose of an interior systems installer is to install, repair, and maintain various elements of the internal structure of buildings. This includes ceilings, walls, partitions, and other interior structures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In their daily work, an employee in this occupation interacts with other colleagues, other trades, site supervisor, site manager, end users, main contractors and suppliers. Their tasks often involve manual labour, such as lifting and installing materials, and may require working at heights using platforms or scaffolding. They will typically report to a supervisor or site manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working environments can vary from internal and external construction sites to occupied buildings such as large commercial properties, residential tower blocks with apartments and specialist buildings such as car showrooms.&amp;nbsp; The work will be physically active, including lifting and fixing systems into place.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This may involve working at height from a platform or mobile scaffold and operatives will follow strict safe working practices at all times in whichever occupational area they choose. They will report to a supervisor or site manager and be capable of managing their own time, quality and resources to meet deadlines and specifications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This occupation follows a core and options standard with two pathway routes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drylining: &lt;/strong&gt;Methods to install various drylining systems that form the walls and rooms within a building, often used to conceal wires and pipes, improve acoustics, and create space for insulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ceiling and Partitions:&lt;/strong&gt; Incorporates different ceiling and partition systems within a building, used to provide various types of working environments, considering lighting and other fixtures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An employee in this occupation will be responsible for managing their time and resources effectively to meet specifications and deadlines. An interior systems installer will also be responsible for being able to read and interpreting instruction and diagrams to ensure that an accurate installation along with testing installed systems to ensure functionality along with adjusting as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
